        "id": 129562,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-27T18:53:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't see how you can play a tactical game against yourself, since you'll always know what your opponent's next move will be (since your opponent is you).</p><p>Someone (phantaskippy?) posted a co-op Tactics scenario to BGG (I think) a while back. &nbsp;It was vs. General Voss attacking Megalopolis and the heroes had to stop the drones destroying the city. &nbsp;Don't know what the feedback was on that scenario, but I loved the idea.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:04:31.438Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
