      {
        "id": 129564,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-27T19:10:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I playtested Tactics solo, because the goal was to find the way each hero played and what they could do, it worked fine.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I understand the frustration with trying to play Tactics solo, because outside of playtesting the solo play kind of stinks. &nbsp;It is doable, but not a lot of fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I would check out my Voss Scenario, and feel free to leave feedback if you do, I have played them a decent bit but they are balanced to my playtesting it, so it may not be balanced well beyond my own play and desired difficulty.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have been working on some more coop-style missions, but there is a real limit to the formats you can use and not have the game stink or be the same as the other scenario.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:04:31.575Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
